# OIBSIP Web Development & Designing
## Level 1 - Task 1: Landing Page

### Project Title
NovaFlow - Productivity Landing Page

### Objective
Build a visually polished static landing page for a product, service, or
brand using HTML5 and CSS3.

This project demonstrates fundamental web development skills including
page structure, layout, typography, navigation, responsive design, and
visual styling.

### Technologies Used
- HTML5
- CSS3
- JavaScript
- Google Fonts
- VS Code
- Live Server

### Features

- Responsive navigation bar
- Hero section with:
  - Main headline
  - Supporting description
  - Call-to-action buttons
- Features section
- About section
- Customer testimonial/review section
- Footer with contact and social links
- Responsive design for desktop, tablet, and mobile screens
- CSS Grid and Flexbox layouts
- Consistent colour palette and typography
- Mobile navigation menu
- Smooth scrolling between sections

### Project Structure

OIBSIP/
└── WebDev-L1-LandingPage/
    ├── index.html
    ├── style.css
    └── README.md

### How to Run

1. Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.
2. Open `index.html`.
3. Right-click inside the HTML file.
4. Select **Open with Live Server**.
5. The landing page will open in your default web browser.

### Project Sections

#### 1. Navigation
The navigation bar provides links to the main sections of the website:
- Features
- About
- Reviews
- Contact

#### 2. Hero Section
The hero section introduces NovaFlow with a main headline,
description, and call-to-action buttons.

#### 3. Features
Three feature cards explain the main benefits of the fictional
NovaFlow productivity platform.

#### 4. About
The About section explains the purpose of the project and the
concept behind the NovaFlow brand.

#### 5. Reviews
A testimonial section demonstrates how customer feedback can be
presented on a landing page.

#### 6. Footer
The footer contains the brand name, contact information, and
social-link placeholders.

### Responsive Design

The website is designed to work on:
- Desktop computers
- Tablets
- Mobile phones

CSS media queries are used to adjust the layout for smaller screens.

